# ============================================================
# EvoNexus — Environment Variables
# ============================================================
# Generated by: make setup
# Edit this file with your API keys.
# ============================================================

# ── Dashboard API Token (for headless agents / CLI) ──
# Bearer token for local agents to call the dashboard API without
# a browser session. Keep it secret — grants full API access.
# Generate with: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# Usage: curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $DASHBOARD_API_TOKEN" ...
#
# On Swarm this comes from the stack's `environment:` section, not this
# file — left commented out on purpose. entrypoint.sh now guards against an
# empty value here clobbering the real one (confirmed live 2026-07-14: a
# blank line here, copied verbatim into the config volume on first boot,
# silently erased the Docker-injected token and broke every API call with
# "Authentication required"), but there's no reason to keep the footgun
# loaded — uncomment and set a value only for non-Swarm/local setups.
# DASHBOARD_API_TOKEN=
# Optional: which user the token impersonates (defaults to first admin)
DASHBOARD_API_USER=

# ── Approval Bridge Token (goal-ticket-unification) ──
# Dedicated credential for POST /api/approvals/{id}/decision — the shared
# Telegram approve/reject gate (publish + sub-goal decomposition). Deliberately
# separate from DASHBOARD_API_TOKEN: an agent inherits its own env, and if the
# approval endpoint accepted the admin token, an agent could approve its own
# publish. Only the dashboard (validates) and the telegram bot in
# TELEGRAM_MODE=provider (sends the decision) should ever have this — never
# the scheduler, which spawns agent subprocesses (see provider_fallback.py
# _build_agent_run_env, which strips it from any agent's env regardless).
# Generate with: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# APPROVAL_BRIDGE_TOKEN=
# Telegram user ids allowed to press an approve/reject button — comma or
# semicolon-separated. Per-individual, not per-chat/group (Vault V3).
# APPROVAL_APPROVER_IDS=

# ── Postiz publish bridge (goal-ticket-unification + social-media-production) ──
# Used only by the dashboard (never by agent subprocesses — POSTIZ_API_KEY is
# denylisted in provider_fallback.py's agent env). POSTIZ_URL is the Postiz
# origin (without /public/v1); POSTIZ_API_KEY is generated in its UI. When
# more than one account exists for a platform, pin the intended one via the
# POSTIZ_INTEGRATION_*_ID vars below (all four platforms MediaJob supports).
# Media referenced by URL (legacy ticket-publish flow) is fail-closed: only
# HTTPS hosts explicitly listed in POSTIZ_ALLOWED_MEDIA_HOSTS are accepted,
# preventing an agent-controlled URL from becoming an SSRF primitive in
# Postiz. MediaJob's own render upload (social-media-production) instead
# streams the local MP4 directly via POST /public/v1/upload — it never goes
# through this URL-allowlist path.
#
# All of the below can also be set via the admin-only, authenticated
# PUT /api/integrations/core/postiz endpoint (masked GET, "keep current on
# blank/masked submit") instead of editing this file by hand — see
# dashboard/backend/routes/integrations_core_postiz.py.
# POSTIZ_URL=https://postiz.example.com
# POSTIZ_API_KEY=
# POSTIZ_INTEGRATION_INSTAGRAM_ID=
# POSTIZ_INTEGRATION_YOUTUBE_ID=
# POSTIZ_INTEGRATION_LINKEDIN_ID=
# POSTIZ_INTEGRATION_TIKTOK_ID=
# Inclua também o host do blog: a ponte Ghost -> redes manda a capa do artigo
# (feature_image) como mídia do Instagram, e ela é servida pelo próprio Ghost.
# POSTIZ_ALLOWED_MEDIA_HOSTS=cdn.example.com,storage.example.com,blog.example.com
# POSTIZ_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
# POSTIZ_UPLOAD_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=900
# POSTIZ_PUBLISH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=90
# POSTIZ_PUBLISH_POLL_SECONDS=3
# Telegram bridge timeout must exceed POSTIZ_PUBLISH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS.
# APPROVAL_DECISION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=105
# Only needed if POSTIZ_URL resolves to a private/internal/loopback address
# (e.g. an internal Swarm alias) — the admin config endpoint's SSRF guard
# blocks those by default. Comma-separated hostnames.
# POSTIZ_URL_ALLOWED_INTERNAL_HOSTS=

# ── social-media-production (MediaJob pipeline: brief -> HyperFrames render
# -> Postiz draft/schedule) ──
# MEDIA_WORKSPACE is a persistent volume shared between the dashboard
# (streaming/upload) and the media-worker service (rendering) — never a
# tmpfs or ephemeral container path. MEDIA_TIMEZONE is the timezone users
# enter scheduled_at in; MediaJob always converts to UTC before calling
# Postiz (never relies on the container's implicit local timezone).
# MEDIA_WORKSPACE=/workspace/media
# MEDIA_TIMEZONE=America/Bahia
# MEDIA_RENDER_CONCURRENCY=1
# MEDIA_JOB_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600
# MEDIA_MAX_FILE_SIZE_BYTES=1073741824
# MEDIA_RETENTION_DAYS=7
# draft: never auto-publishes (default, safe for smoke tests). schedule:
# allowed only once a job is approved, has a future scheduled_at, and the
# target Postiz integration is active — see routes/media_jobs.py's /schedule.
# SOCIAL_DEFAULT_POST_MODE=draft

# ── MinIO / S3 media host (int-minio skill, Option A) ──
# Publishing agents upload generated media here and pass the public URL to
# Postiz. The bucket must allow public read (bucket policy). Unlike
# POSTIZ_API_KEY, MINIO_* IS available to agent subprocesses — they need it to
# upload (uploading to a bucket is not the publish action; the Instagram post
# itself still requires human approval). Whatever host serves the public URL
# must also appear in POSTIZ_ALLOWED_MEDIA_HOSTS above.
# MINIO_ENDPOINT=https://s3.example.com
# MINIO_ACCESS_KEY=
# MINIO_SECRET_KEY=
# MINIO_BUCKET=post
# MINIO_PUBLIC_BASE=https://s3.example.com
# MINIO_SET_PUBLIC_ACL=0

# Dashboard session secret. Required in production.
EVONEXUS_SECRET_KEY=

# ── Dashboard resource limits (VPS / Docker Swarm) ──
# Override defaults via Portainer env vars when deploying the stack.
# EVONEXUS_DASHBOARD_CPUS: max CPUs for the dashboard container
#   (default 2 — dashboard runs Flask + terminal-server + agent PTYs)
# EVONEXUS_DASHBOARD_MEMORY: max memory for the dashboard container
#   (default 2048M — 1GB crashes with 2-3 agent tabs open)
# EVONEXUS_DASHBOARD_CPUS=2
# EVONEXUS_DASHBOARD_MEMORY=2048M

# ── Terminal-server guard-rails ──
# Max simultaneous Claude/openclaude PTY sessions (each uses 200-400MB).
# Old sessions without an active viewer are reaped after the TTL expires.
# TERMINAL_MAX_ACTIVE_SESSIONS=4
# TERMINAL_DETACHED_TTL_MINUTES=30

# Comma-separated list of allowed browser origins for the Flask dashboard.
# Use "*" for local development; set explicit origins in production.
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=*

# ── AI Provider Configuration ────────────────────────
# EvoNexus supports multiple AI providers via OpenClaude.
# Configure via dashboard (Providers page) or edit config/providers.json.
# The active provider determines which CLI (claude or openclaude) is used.
#
# HOW KEY RESOLUTION WORKS (read this before debugging a 401):
#   1. Each provider entry in config/providers.json has its own env_vars —
#      including its own OPENAI_API_KEY. That key ALWAYS wins for that
#      provider. The Providers page in the dashboard writes it for you.
#   2. Keys below in this .env are FALLBACKS, used only when the provider
#      entry has no usable key (empty or "[REDACTED]" placeholder).
#   3. NVIDIA_API_KEY from this .env is only applied to *.nvidia.com
#      endpoints — it is never sent to other gateways.
# So: to fix an invalid/expired key for one provider, update it on the
# Providers page (or in config/providers.json), not here.
#
# Anthropic (default): no extra config needed — uses native 'claude' CLI.
#
# OpenRouter (200+ models) — key: https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys
#   CLAUDE_CODE_USE_OPENAI=1
#   OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-or-...
#   OPENAI_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4
#
# OpenAI — key: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#   CLAUDE_CODE_USE_OPENAI=1
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
#   OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4.1
#
# Google Gemini — key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#   CLAUDE_CODE_USE_GEMINI=1
#   GEMINI_API_KEY=...
#   GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro
#
# NVIDIA NIM — key: https://build.nvidia.com (Get API Key on any model page)
#   CLAUDE_CODE_USE_OPENAI=1
#   OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
#   NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-...
#   OPENAI_MODEL=<model id from build.nvidia.com>
#
# OmniRoute (self-hosted gateway, 237+ providers with auto-fallback):
#   Deploy: https://github.com/diegosouzapw/OmniRoute — see the optional
#   `omniroute` service in evonexus-vps.stack.example.yml.
#   Key: OmniRoute dashboard → Endpoints → create an API key (sk-...).
#   Keys are stored in OmniRoute's SQLite volume — wiping the volume
#   invalidates every key; generate a new one after a reset.
#   CLAUDE_CODE_USE_OPENAI=1
#   OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://omniroute:20128/v1   # Swarm-internal DNS alias
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...                        # key from the step above
#   OPENAI_MODEL=auto                            # let OmniRoute route+fallback
#
# Install openclaude for non-Anthropic providers:
#   npm install -g @gitlawb/openclaude

# ── Omie ERP ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Omie API (omie.com.br → Settings → Integrations → API)
OMIE_APP_KEY=
OMIE_APP_SECRET=

# ── Bling ERP ────────────────────────────────────────
# Bling API v3 — OAuth2 with automatic refresh.
# 1. Create an app at https://developer.bling.com.br
# 2. Set redirect URI to: http://localhost:8787/callback
# 3. Paste Client ID/Secret below, then run `make bling-auth` to complete login.
# The CLI opens your browser, captures the code, and fills ACCESS/REFRESH tokens here.
BLING_CLIENT_ID=
BLING_CLIENT_SECRET=
BLING_ACCESS_TOKEN=
BLING_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# ── Asaas (payments) ─────────────────────────────────
# Asaas API key (account settings → Integrations → API Key)
# Set ASAAS_SANDBOX=true to hit sandbox.asaas.com (safe default)
ASAAS_API_KEY=
ASAAS_SANDBOX=true

# ── Stripe ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Stripe Secret Key (dashboard.stripe.com → Developers → API Keys)
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# ── Todoist ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Todoist API Token (app.todoist.com → Settings → Integrations → API Token)
TODOIST_API_TOKEN=

# ── Fathom (Meetings) ───────────────────────────────
# Fathom API Key (fathom.video → Settings → API)
FATHOM_API_KEY=

# ── Discord ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Discord Bot Token (discord.com/developers → Bot → Token)
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=
# Server Guild ID (enable Developer Mode → right-click server → Copy ID)
DISCORD_GUILD_ID=

# ── Telegram ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Bot Token from @BotFather
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Chat ID (send /start to your bot, check via getUpdates API)
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ── YouTube OAuth ────────────────────────────────────
# Google Cloud Console → APIs → Credentials → OAuth Client
YOUTUBE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
YOUTUBE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Meta / Instagram OAuth ───────────────────────────
# Facebook App (developers.facebook.com → My Apps → Settings → Basic)
META_APP_ID=
META_APP_SECRET=

# ── LinkedIn OAuth ───────────────────────────────────
# LinkedIn App (linkedin.com/developers → My Apps → Auth)
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID=
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── License — headless auto-activation ───────────────
# Set this to the email used in your first manual license registration.
# On startup, EvoNexus calls /v1/register/auto silently and skips the manual
# setup screen. Falls back to manual setup if the email isn't registered yet.
# Leave empty (or unset) to keep the default behavior.
# EVOLUTION_OPERATOR_EMAIL=operator@example.com

# ── Evolution API ────────────────────────────────────
# Your Evolution API instance URL and global API key
EVOLUTION_API_URL=
EVOLUTION_API_KEY=

# ── Evolution Go ─────────────────────────────────────
# Your Evolution Go instance URL and API key
EVOLUTION_GO_URL=
EVOLUTION_GO_KEY=
# WhatsApp instance to send FROM (Evolution Go). Defaults to "sistema-britto"
# in code if unset — override only if your instance is named differently.
EVOLUTION_GO_INSTANCE=
# Superadmin's WhatsApp number to send TO (E.164 without "+", e.g. 5511999999999).
# Used by the Operacional-diário routines (Review Todoist, Email Triage,
# Sync Meetings, Status Diário) and by daily_status_report.py.
WHATSAPP_PHONE=

# ── Evo AI CRM ──────────────────────────────────────
# Your Evo AI CRM instance URL and access token
EVO_CRM_URL=
EVO_CRM_TOKEN=

# ── Backup (S3-compatible) ───────────────────────────
# S3 bucket for remote backups (any S3-compatible: AWS, MinIO, R2, etc.)
BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=
# Prefix/folder inside the bucket (default: evonexus-backups/)
BACKUP_S3_PREFIX=evonexus-backups/
# AWS credentials (or S3-compatible endpoint)
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=           # For non-AWS (MinIO, R2, etc.)
# Retention: how many backups to keep (empty = unlimited)
# BACKUP_RETAIN_LOCAL=7       # Keep last 7 local backups
# BACKUP_RETAIN_S3=30         # Keep last 30 S3 backups

# ── Social Accounts ──────────────────────────────────
# Managed via the dashboard Integrations page.
# Pattern: SOCIAL_{PLATFORM}_{N}_{FIELD}
# Example:
# SOCIAL_YOUTUBE_1_LABEL=My Channel
# SOCIAL_YOUTUBE_1_ACCESS_TOKEN=ya29...
# SOCIAL_YOUTUBE_1_CHANNEL_ID=UC...

# -- AI Image Creator (image generation) ----------------
# Cloudflare AI Gateway mode (recommended):
AI_IMG_CREATOR_CF_ACCOUNT_ID=
AI_IMG_CREATOR_CF_GATEWAY_ID=
AI_IMG_CREATOR_CF_TOKEN=
# Direct API keys (simpler alternative):
AI_IMG_CREATOR_OPENROUTER_KEY=
AI_IMG_CREATOR_GEMINI_KEY=

# ── Knowledge Base — Embedder (optional) ────────────
# The Knowledge Base (pgvector) uses one of three embedders:
#   local   — sentence-transformers/paraphrase-multilingual-mpnet-base-v2 (default)
#             768 dim · offline · ~420 MB model download on first use
#   openai  — text-embedding-3-small / -3-large / ada-002
#             1536 or 3072 dim · requires OPENAI_API_KEY
#   gemini  — gemini-embedding-001 (stable) or gemini-embedding-2-preview
#             768 / 1536 / 3072 dim (MRL) · requires GEMINI_API_KEY
#
# Most users should configure this via the dashboard at /knowledge/settings
# rather than editing .env directly. The provider is locked once the first
# connection is created.
#
# KNOWLEDGE_EMBEDDER_PROVIDER=local
#
# -- Gemini embedder ----------------------------------
# Get a free key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey (generous free tier).
# GEMINI_API_KEY=AIzaSy...
# KNOWLEDGE_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-embedding-001   # or gemini-embedding-2-preview
# KNOWLEDGE_GEMINI_DIM=768                      # 768 (default, aligns with local), 1536, or 3072


# -- Databases (db-postgres, db-mysql) ----------------
# Numbered blocks — one per database. Same pattern as SOCIAL_YOUTUBE_N_*.
# Skills pick connections by LABEL (case-insensitive) or numeric index.
# LABEL is the only required field. DSN, if set, wins over component fields.
# Read-only by default — set ALLOW_WRITE=true per connection to permit writes.
#
# Drivers are NOT pre-installed. First use:
#   uv pip install psycopg2-binary   # for db-postgres
#   uv pip install pymysql           # for db-mysql
#
# ── Postgres ─────────────────────────────────────────
# DB_POSTGRES_1_LABEL=msgops-dev
# DB_POSTGRES_1_HOST=db.dev.internal
# DB_POSTGRES_1_PORT=5432
# DB_POSTGRES_1_DATABASE=msgops
# DB_POSTGRES_1_USER=agent_readonly
# DB_POSTGRES_1_PASSWORD=
# DB_POSTGRES_1_SSL_MODE=require             # disable | require | verify-ca | verify-full
# DB_POSTGRES_1_SSL_CA_PATH=                 # optional, if verify-*
# DB_POSTGRES_1_ALLOW_WRITE=false
# DB_POSTGRES_1_QUERY_TIMEOUT=30
# DB_POSTGRES_1_MAX_ROWS=1000
#
# Or a full DSN alternative (DSN wins over components):
# DB_POSTGRES_2_LABEL=evo-ai-dev
# DB_POSTGRES_2_DSN=postgresql://user:pw@host:5432/db?sslmode=require
#
# ── MySQL / MariaDB ──────────────────────────────────
# DB_MYSQL_1_LABEL=orders-dev
# DB_MYSQL_1_HOST=mysql.dev.internal
# DB_MYSQL_1_PORT=3306
# DB_MYSQL_1_DATABASE=orders
# DB_MYSQL_1_USER=agent_readonly
# DB_MYSQL_1_PASSWORD=
# DB_MYSQL_1_SSL_CA_PATH=                    # optional, enables TLS verification
# DB_MYSQL_1_ALLOW_WRITE=false
# DB_MYSQL_1_QUERY_TIMEOUT=30
# DB_MYSQL_1_MAX_ROWS=1000
#
# ── MongoDB ──────────────────────────────────────────
# DB_MONGO_1_LABEL=orders-dev
# DB_MONGO_1_URI=mongodb+srv://user:pw@cluster0.abc.mongodb.net/orders?retryWrites=true
# # Or components instead of URI:
# # DB_MONGO_1_HOST=mongo.dev.internal
# # DB_MONGO_1_PORT=27017
# # DB_MONGO_1_DATABASE=orders
# # DB_MONGO_1_USER=agent_readonly
# # DB_MONGO_1_PASSWORD=
# # DB_MONGO_1_AUTH_SOURCE=admin
# # DB_MONGO_1_TLS=true
# DB_MONGO_1_ALLOW_WRITE=false
# DB_MONGO_1_QUERY_TIMEOUT=30
# DB_MONGO_1_MAX_ROWS=1000
#
# ── Redis ────────────────────────────────────────────
# DB_REDIS_1_LABEL=cache-dev
# DB_REDIS_1_URL=rediss://user:pw@host:6380/0
# # Or components instead of URL:
# # DB_REDIS_1_HOST=redis.dev.internal
# # DB_REDIS_1_PORT=6379
# # DB_REDIS_1_DB=0
# # DB_REDIS_1_USERNAME=
# # DB_REDIS_1_PASSWORD=
# # DB_REDIS_1_TLS=false
# DB_REDIS_1_ALLOW_WRITE=false
# DB_REDIS_1_QUERY_TIMEOUT=30
# DB_REDIS_1_MAX_ROWS=1000

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# OpenSEO (plugin open-seo) — camada de dados de SEO self-hosted
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Sobe via `docker compose up -d open-seo` (imagem oficial ghcr.io/every-app/
# open-seo). O MCP fica em ${OPEN_SEO_URL}/mcp e já está registrado no
# .mcp.json como `plugin-open-seo-openseo`. Detalhes: plugins/open-seo/README.md
#
# DATAFORSEO_API_KEY é a ÚNICA obrigatória e a única que custa dinheiro: o
# OpenSEO é a UI/MCP, quem devolve dado de SEO é o DataForSEO (pay-as-you-go,
# cobrado direto na sua conta). Sem ela o serviço sobe mas toda query volta
# vazia. Formato: base64 de "login:senha" — ver docs/DATAFORSEO_API_KEY.md no
# upstream ou https://dataforseo.com
# DATAFORSEO_API_KEY=
#
# Porta publicada (só em 127.0.0.1 — AUTH_MODE=local_noauth não tem login,
# nunca exponha isso na internet sem trocar o modo de auth antes).
# OPEN_SEO_PORT=3001
# OPEN_SEO_IMAGE=ghcr.io/every-app/open-seo:latest
# OPEN_SEO_ALLOWED_HOST=
# OPENSEO_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1
#
# Opcional — conectar o Google Search Console (dados de 1ª parte: queries que
# já rendem impressão, termos em "striking distance"). Sem isso as skills de
# keyword research funcionam, só perdem essa fonte.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# x.ai (Grok) — pesquisa em tempo real com acesso ao X
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NÃO confundir com a API da rede social X (console.x.com, usada para postar).
# Esta é o LLM Grok, do console.x.ai — produtos diferentes, consoles diferentes.
# Publicação no X não usa esta chave: vai pelo Postiz (social-schedule-postiz).
#
# Usada para complementar levantamento de tendências/notícias com o sinal do X,
# onde a discussão de IA aparece antes de virar artigo. Chave no formato xai-...
# Exige créditos no time (console.x.ai/team/<id>) — sem saldo a API responde
# permission-denied com team_blocked=true, mesmo com a chave válida.
# XAI_API_KEY=
# XAI_BASE_URL=https://api.x.ai/v1

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Endereço público do Nexus — links de aprovação no Telegram
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# O card de aprovação manda um link para /approvals, e o request.host_url
# atrás de um proxy reverso é o host interno do container — um link para
# http://evonexus-dashboard:8080 não abre no celular de ninguém. NGROK_URL é
# aceito como alternativa por já existir em instalações antigas.
# NEXUS_PUBLIC_URL=https://nexus.example.com

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Ponte Ghost -> redes sociais
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Folga entre publicar o artigo no blog e o primeiro post da rede sair, em
# horas. Serve para rever o artigo já publicado antes de apontar tráfego para
# ele; as redes seguintes saem escalonadas depois dessa (ver OFFSET_MIN em
# dashboard/backend/ghost_social_bridge.py). Default 2.
# GHOST_SOCIAL_DELAY_HOURS=2

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Ponte de aprovação do Telegram — OBRIGATÓRIA para os botões funcionarem
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Credencial dedicada do bot para chamar POST /api/approvals/<id>/decision.
# Deliberadamente NÃO é o DASHBOARD_API_TOKEN: muitos agentes carregam aquele
# token via EvoClient, e reusá-lo aqui deixaria um agente aprovar o próprio
# gate de publicação.
#
# Sem ela o sistema fica fail-closed e SILENCIOSO do lado de fora: o dashboard
# recusa toda requisição da ponte e o bot responde "Bridge de aprovação não
# configurado neste serviço" — os três botões (aprovar / ajustar / rejeitar)
# simplesmente não fazem nada. Gere com:
#     python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
# O MESMO valor precisa estar visível para o serviço do dashboard E para o do
# Telegram (no Swarm os dois montam o volume de config, então basta o .env).
# APPROVAL_BRIDGE_TOKEN=
#
# Quem pode DECIDIR uma aprovação: ids de USUÁRIO do Telegram, separados por
# vírgula. Não é id de chat/grupo — aprovar publicação não pode depender de
# quem estava na conversa. O servidor deriva `decided_by` do from_id recebido,
# então esta lista é a última checagem antes de confiar naquele valor.
# Vazia, toda decisão volta 403 "not an approver" — e, como o token acima,
# isso só aparece quando alguém aperta o botão. Descubra seu id conversando
# com @userinfobot no Telegram.
# APPROVAL_APPROVER_IDS=123456789

# crawl4ai — camada de crawling (stack `crawl4ai`, crawl.workflowapi.com.br).
# A imagem sobe em 127.0.0.1 e SÓ abre para a rede quando este token existe:
# é o entrypoint que decide o bind a partir dele. Sem o token o serviço sobe,
# responde no localhost dele, e nem o Traefik alcança.
CRAWL4AI_API_TOKEN=

# mcp-reddit — dor do cliente na palavra dele, para gancho de pauta.
#
# Sem credencial NÃO funciona na VPS: o www.reddit.com devolve 403 para IP de
# datacenter, com ou sem User-Agent (medido em 2026-07-26). Com OAuth a
# chamada sai por oauth.reddit.com, que não aplica esse bloqueio.
#
# Como obter, uma vez:
#   1. https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps -> "create another app..."
#   2. tipo "script", redirect URI http://localhost:8080
#   3. CLIENT_ID é a string sob o nome do app; SECRET é o campo "secret"
#   4. o refresh token sai do fluxo OAuth do próprio app (escopo "read")
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
REDDIT_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Senha do admin de sistemabritto.com.br — leitura das métricas de crescimento.
# O site já registra pageviews com utm_source, cliques de CTA e o pipeline de
# leads em Supabase; a rotina daily_growth_metrics lê por /api/admin e grava a
# série histórica no Nexus. Só leitura: nada é escrito no site.
SITE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Trocar apenas se o domínio mudar.
SITE_ADMIN_URL=https://www.sistemabritto.com.br
